\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The Lord's my shepherd, I'll not want; 
\par He make me down to lie 
\par In pastures green; he leadeth me 
\par The quiet waters by.
\par   \tab 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. My soul he doth restore again, 
\par And me to walk doth make 
\par Within the paths of righteousness,
\par E'en for His own name's sake. 
\par \pard\tx1850\tab 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Yea, though I walk in death's dark vale,
\par Yet will I fear no ill;
\par For Thou art with me, and Thy rod 
\par And staff me comfort still. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. My table Thou hast furnished 
\par In the presence of my foes;
\par My head Thou dost with oil anoint, 
\par And my cup overflows. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Goodness and mercy all my life 
\par Shall surely follow me, 
\par And in God's house forever more
\par My dwelling-place shall be. 
\par 
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

